# cliphist -- clipboard history daemon settings.
#
# Format is `key value`, one per line, with NO leading dash. This is not
# documented anywhere; it was determined by experiment. `-db-path ./x` and
# `db-path=./x` both parse as nothing and are silently ignored, which is the
# worst possible failure mode -- so if a setting here seems to do nothing,
# suspect the syntax before suspecting cliphist.
#
# These are the same names shown by `cliphist -h`, minus the dash. Reading
# this file replaces command-line flags, so every cliphist invocation --
# the watchers in conf/autostart.lua and clip-menu alike -- picks these up
# without repeating them.

# 750 (the default) is far more history than is ever scrolled through, and
# every entry is a row rofi has to render. 200 still covers days of work.
max-items 200

# How much of each entry is shown in the picker. The default 100 truncates
# mid-path on anything long; clip-menu opens a 52em-wide window, so there is
# room for more.
preview-width 180

# db-path is deliberately left at its default, ~/.cache/cliphist/db.
#
# It is arguably state rather than cache, but Go does not expand `~` in a
# config value, so overriding it would mean hardcoding /home/barinder into a
# file that is meant to be portable. Living under ~/.cache also means a cache
# cleaner erases the clipboard history, which for clipboard history is a
# feature. The file itself is mode 644, but ~/.cache and ~/.cache/cliphist are
# both 700, so no other local user can reach it.
